			"notes": "Beta on every loader and version. Requires Xaero's World Map; the mod must also be installed on the server.\n\n- Players who left before you joined now appear on your map. The server remembers the last position of players who were sharing (dimension, time since they left, skin) for 7 days and sends it when you join. It is saved with the world, so a server restart keeps it.\n- Privacy: when you share your position, your last position stays visible to the players you chose for 7 days after you leave, or until you come back. Turning the game rule `xaeroheadtracker:allow_sharing` off erases all stored positions.\n- Players you never saw now show their real skin (or Steve/Alex) instead of a red square.\n- After 60 minutes, the time since a player left is shown in hours.\n- Fabric and NeoForge 26.3 with Xaero's Minimap: a nearby player is only left to the Minimap when its radar really draws them on the world map (before, nearby players could disappear).\n- Fabric 1.21.x includes the 2.2.1 Java 21 fix.\n\nCompatible with 2.2.x clients and servers (the new data is optional), but the server and the players need 2.3.0 to see players who left.\n\nFabric now lives on a single branch, `v2/fabric/all`, which builds 26.3, 26.2, 1.21.11 and 1.21.1."
		},
